"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNotations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Notations refer to musical notations, not XML notations. Multiple notations are allowed in order to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiple editorial levels. The print-object attribute, added in Version 3.0, allows notations to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"details of performance technique, such as fingerings, without having them appear in the score.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations","title":"MXLNotations","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLDynamics":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxldynamics","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLDynamics","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLDynamics","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Dynamics can be associated either with a note or a general musical direction. To avoid inconsistencies between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and among the letter abbreviations for dynamics (what is sf vs. sfz, standing alone or with a trailing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamic that is not always piano), we use the actual letters as the names of these dynamic elements. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other-dynamics element allows other dynamic marks that are not covered here. Dynamics elements may also be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combined to create marks not covered by a single element, such as sfmp.","